1
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,600
So? You gonna make me stand here all day, or what?

2
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:29,179
Girl. Girl!

3
00:01:45,504 --> 00:01:47,183
Question four got me too.

4
00:01:47,444 --> 00:01:48,654
You got an A.

5
00:01:48,704 --> 00:01:49,694
I saw it.

6
00:01:49,743 --> 00:01:50,743
Yeah.

7
00:01:51,243 --> 00:01:52,304
But it hurt.

8
00:01:52,664 --> 00:01:55,804
I need a B to keep my spot in the summer program at the hospital.

9
00:01:55,944 --> 00:01:58,934
If I don't get it, my grandma's gonna act like she's not disappointed,

10
00:01:58,984 --> 00:02:00,183
and that's worse.

11
00:02:00,963 --> 00:02:03,614
I'm at the library Tuesdays and Thursdays after school.

12
00:02:03,664 --> 00:02:04,664
If you want.

13
00:02:04,784 --> 00:02:05,784
No pressure.

14
00:02:06,124 --> 00:02:07,304
You tutor people?

15
00:02:07,984 --> 00:02:08,774
Not really.

16
00:02:08,824 --> 00:02:10,884
I just explain stuff to myself out loud.

17
00:02:11,124 --> 00:02:13,164
You'd just be listening.

18
00:03:00,364 --> 00:03:02,304
How do you know I don't eat the crust?

19
00:03:02,484 --> 00:03:04,584
You've been peeling it off for three weeks.

20
00:03:05,063 --> 00:03:06,244
It's kind of loud.

21
00:03:06,524 --> 00:03:08,084
It's not loud.

22
00:03:08,644 --> 00:03:10,064
It's a little loud.

23
00:03:29,003 --> 00:03:31,184
Get in. You're getting soaked.

24
00:03:32,144 --> 00:03:33,144
I'm good.

25
00:03:33,984 --> 00:03:35,664
You're literally dripping.

26
00:03:36,304 --> 00:03:38,224
Come on. I don't bite. Usually.

27
00:03:42,693 --> 00:03:43,944
You sing, right?

28
00:03:44,283 --> 00:03:44,774
Choir.

29
00:03:44,824 --> 00:03:46,924
Front row, left side.

30
00:03:47,604 --> 00:03:48,804
You noticed that?

31
00:03:49,424 --> 00:03:50,744
I notice a lot.

32
00:03:51,503 --> 00:03:53,344
I just don't say it to everybody.

33
00:03:54,044 --> 00:03:56,144
You say everything to everybody, Trey.

34
00:03:56,504 --> 00:03:57,964
Okay, that's fair.

35
00:04:02,224 --> 00:04:03,564
Thank you.

36
00:04:03,843 --> 00:04:04,753
For real.

37
00:04:04,804 --> 00:04:05,804
You're welcome.

38
00:04:05,984 --> 00:04:06,984
For real.

39
00:04:18,733 --> 00:04:21,774
So which one gave you that look on your face?

40
00:04:22,454 --> 00:04:23,514
What look?

41
00:04:24,574 --> 00:04:25,674
That one.

42
00:04:25,814 --> 00:04:28,394
The one I had in nineteen seventy-four.

43
00:04:30,473 --> 00:04:31,814
There's this boy, Malik.

44
00:04:32,514 --> 00:04:33,954
He helps me with calculus.

45
00:04:34,874 --> 00:04:37,473
He's sweet, Grandma. Like, quiet sweet.

46
00:04:37,553 --> 00:04:38,834
He notices everything.

47
00:04:39,673 --> 00:04:41,153
And then there's Trey.

48
00:04:42,254 --> 00:04:44,634
He's loud, and he's kind of full of himself.

49
00:04:45,473 --> 00:04:48,434
But when he looks at me, it's like nobody else is in the room.

50
00:04:48,894 --> 00:04:50,294
Baby, listen to me.

51
00:04:50,954 --> 00:04:53,674
Don't pick the boy who makes you feel lucky.

52
00:04:54,533 --> 00:04:57,194
Pick the one who makes you feel like yourself.

53
00:05:19,614 --> 00:05:21,894
You were not supposed to see me like this.

54
00:05:22,473 --> 00:05:23,473
Like what?

55
00:05:23,813 --> 00:05:24,813
Working?

56
00:05:25,053 --> 00:05:26,494
You're here every weekend?

57
00:05:27,033 --> 00:05:28,033
Every weekend.

58
00:05:28,533 --> 00:05:32,074
My mom does mornings at the hospital laundry, and nights at the diner.

59
00:05:32,353 --> 00:05:34,014
I do Saturdays and Sundays.

60
00:05:34,813 --> 00:05:36,653
Between the two of us, the lights stay on.

61
00:05:37,274 --> 00:05:38,543
You never told me any of that.

62
00:05:38,593 --> 00:05:40,713
You never asked.

63
00:05:41,553 --> 00:05:43,194
And it's not a sad story.

64
00:05:43,933 --> 00:05:45,174
It's just my story.

65
00:06:00,454 --> 00:06:02,334
Thirty-one points.

66
00:06:03,233 --> 00:06:04,934
Everybody's talking about you.

67
00:06:05,933 --> 00:06:07,194
Not everybody.

68
00:06:08,014 --> 00:06:09,494
My dad's seat.

69
00:06:10,293 --> 00:06:11,483
He's never sat in it.

70
00:06:11,533 --> 00:06:12,533
Not once.

71
00:06:12,713 --> 00:06:13,713
Four years.

72
00:06:18,793 --> 00:06:19,793
Trey.

73
00:06:20,014 --> 00:06:21,473
He sends money.

74
00:06:22,074 --> 00:06:23,774
That's his way of saying he was there.

75
00:06:24,494 --> 00:06:26,074
That's not the same thing.

76
00:06:26,213 --> 00:06:27,103
Yeah.

77
00:06:27,153 --> 00:06:28,153
I know.

78
00:06:42,394 --> 00:06:44,473
Trey Whitfield sat with you after the game?

79
00:06:44,553 --> 00:06:46,363
Girl, are you serious right now?

80
00:06:46,413 --> 00:06:48,684
It's not like that. And Malik is,

81
00:06:48,734 --> 00:06:49,603
Malik is nice.

82
00:06:49,653 --> 00:06:50,503
Malik is real nice.

83
00:06:50,553 --> 00:06:52,174
But nice doesn't pick you up in the rain.

84
00:07:03,593 --> 00:07:05,213
Just ask her, baby.

85
00:07:07,874 --> 00:07:09,093
Ask her to what?

86
00:07:09,153 --> 00:07:10,634
Ride on my handlebars to prom?

87
00:07:11,014 --> 00:07:12,603
She's not looking at your shoes, Malik.

88
00:07:12,653 --> 00:07:13,774
She's looking at you.

89
00:07:24,202 --> 00:07:27,302
So? You gonna make me stand here all day, or what?

90
00:07:36,562 --> 00:07:38,763
Can I think about it?

91
00:07:40,942 --> 00:07:41,932
Take your time.

92
00:07:41,983 --> 00:07:44,453
I'm not going anywhere.

93
00:07:58,862 --> 00:07:59,983
Mama.

94
00:08:03,783 --> 00:08:05,143
What is this?

95
00:08:05,763 --> 00:08:07,343
The building got sold.

96
00:08:07,903 --> 00:08:09,483
We have sixty days.

97
00:08:34,562 --> 00:08:35,903
Sixty days.

98
00:08:36,623 --> 00:08:38,342
That's what your family gave mine.

99
00:08:39,003 --> 00:08:39,913
What are you talking about?

100
00:08:39,962 --> 00:08:41,423
Read it.

101
00:08:42,423 --> 00:08:43,722
Read the name at the bottom.

102
00:08:47,043 --> 00:08:48,362
Man, I didn't know about this.

103
00:08:48,863 --> 00:08:50,342
I don't run my dad's company.

104
00:08:50,722 --> 00:08:51,722
No.

105
00:08:52,023 --> 00:08:53,473
You just drive it to school.

106
00:08:53,523 --> 00:08:54,213
Stop!

107
00:08:54,263 --> 00:08:55,822
Both of you, stop.

108
00:09:13,322 --> 00:09:15,142
Malik. Talk to me.

109
00:09:15,623 --> 00:09:16,842
What is there to say?

110
00:09:17,822 --> 00:09:19,502
He can give you everything.

111
00:09:20,423 --> 00:09:22,362
I can barely give my mom rent money.

112
00:09:22,923 --> 00:09:24,702
Did I ever ask you for anything?

113
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:26,523
No.

114
00:09:26,903 --> 00:09:27,923
You never did.

115
00:09:28,503 --> 00:09:29,742
That's what makes it worse.

116
00:09:31,763 --> 00:09:33,762
You belong in his world, Zara.

117
00:09:34,003 --> 00:09:35,102
Not mine.

118
00:09:35,623 --> 00:09:37,163
Don't tell me where I belong.

119
00:09:37,883 --> 00:09:39,423
I'm not trying to hurt you.

120
00:09:40,062 --> 00:09:42,342
I'm trying to stop hurting myself.

121
00:10:00,623 --> 00:10:01,762
I'm sorry.

122
00:10:01,942 --> 00:10:04,173
I kept pushing you toward Trey because I liked him.

123
00:10:04,222 --> 00:10:05,362
I should have told you.

124
00:10:05,822 --> 00:10:07,702
Of course you did.

125
00:10:19,042 --> 00:10:20,782
The Eastside building.

126
00:10:21,822 --> 00:10:23,162
People live there, Dad.

127
00:10:23,682 --> 00:10:25,621
A kid from my school lives there.

128
00:10:26,282 --> 00:10:27,461
It's business, son.

129
00:10:27,862 --> 00:10:29,641
You'll understand one day.

130
00:10:29,782 --> 00:10:31,442
You never came to one game.

131
00:10:31,961 --> 00:10:33,042
Not one.

132
00:10:34,282 --> 00:10:36,841
Four years, and that seat was always empty.

133
00:10:40,961 --> 00:10:47,062
I stopped asking you to show up for me. But don't take their home too.

134
00:10:47,341 --> 00:10:48,822
Watch your tone in my house.

135
00:10:50,922 --> 00:10:52,141
Keep the car.

136
00:10:52,262 --> 00:10:52,892
Keep all of it.

137
00:10:52,942 --> 00:10:54,001
Just stop the deal.

138
00:11:21,042 --> 00:11:22,761
They pulled out.

139
00:11:23,221 --> 00:11:24,372
The sale's off.

140
00:11:24,422 --> 00:11:25,422
We can stay.

141
00:11:25,742 --> 00:11:26,312
What?

142
00:11:26,362 --> 00:11:27,272
Why?

143
00:11:27,322 --> 00:11:28,332
It doesn't say.

144
00:11:28,382 --> 00:11:30,001
It just says we can stay.

145
00:11:58,642 --> 00:11:59,642
So?

146
00:12:00,081 --> 00:12:01,121
Which one?

147
00:12:02,002 --> 00:12:03,621
I don't know, Grandma.

148
00:12:03,862 --> 00:12:05,381
Yes, you do.

149
00:12:05,662 --> 00:12:08,182
You just don't want to hurt the other one.

150
00:12:25,481 --> 00:12:27,701
I didn't hear your car.

151
00:12:28,602 --> 00:12:29,781
I took a ride share.

152
00:12:30,362 --> 00:12:31,362
Long story.

153
00:12:32,162 --> 00:12:33,241
It was you.

154
00:12:33,922 --> 00:12:34,922
Malik's building.

155
00:12:35,522 --> 00:12:36,562
Don't tell him.

156
00:12:37,362 --> 00:12:38,621
He'd hate owing me.

157
00:12:44,142 --> 00:12:46,802
I should have given you this six weeks ago.

158
00:12:57,741 --> 00:12:59,041
I know.

159
00:13:00,461 --> 00:13:02,562
I saw your face when he walked in.

160
00:13:04,602 --> 00:13:05,552
Trey, I,

161
00:13:05,602 --> 00:13:06,621
Don't.

162
00:13:07,481 --> 00:13:08,981
You don't owe me a speech.

163
00:13:09,902 --> 00:13:11,101
She's worth it.

164
00:13:11,862 --> 00:13:13,822
Make sure she knows it.

165
00:13:14,201 --> 00:13:15,201
Every day.

166
00:13:21,322 --> 00:13:22,822
I can't really dance.

167
00:13:23,522 --> 00:13:24,522
I know.

168
00:13:24,942 --> 00:13:26,101
It's kind of loud.

169
00:13:53,102 --> 00:13:54,841
I cancelled the deal.

170
00:13:57,302 --> 00:13:58,981
And I watched the tape of your game.

171
00:13:59,522 --> 00:14:00,012
All of it.

172
00:14:00,062 --> 00:14:00,792
Thirty-one points.

173
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:04,900
I should have been in that seat, son.
